questions.question:
main.ts registers app.useGlobalPipes(new ValidationPipe()). The controller and the service:

@Post()
enroll(@Body() dto: EnrollRequestDto) {
  return this.enrollments.enroll(dto);
}

// EnrollmentService.enroll starts with: this.logger.log(`enroll ${dto.courseId}`);

A request without an email:

POST /v1/enrollments  {"courseId":"sql-data-modeling","plan":"free"}
HTTP/1.1 400  {"message":["email must be an email"],"error":"Bad Request","statusCode":400}

The application log for that request has no "enroll sql-data-modeling" line.

Statement: "The 400 was produced by the ValidationPipe before the controller method ran, so EnrollmentService.enroll was never called with this body."

main.ts registers app.useGlobalPipes(new ValidationPipe()) with no options. A route in CoursesController:

@Get(':id/lessons')
lessons(@Param('id') id: number) {
  this.logger.log(`typeof id = ${typeof id}`);
  return this.courses.lessonsOf(id);
}

Request: GET /v1/courses/42/lessons

Statement: "Because the parameter is declared as id: number, Nest converts \"42\" to the number 42 before calling lessons(), and the log line says typeof id = number."
